# Conventional Commits

When drafting or creating a git commit message, follow [Conventional Commits 1.0.0](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/en/v1.0.0/).

```
<type>[optional scope]: <description>

[optional body]

[optional footer(s)]
```

- Subject: lowercase type, optional scope in parentheses, colon, space, then a short imperative description.
- Keep the subject under 72 characters.
- Put a blank line before the body. Use the body for why, not a restatement of the diff.
- Allowed types: `feat`, `fix`, `refactor`, `docs`, `test`, `chore`, `style`, `perf`, `build`, `ci`.
- `feat` for a new feature, `fix` for a bug fix. Mark a breaking change with `!` before the colon or a `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer.

```
feat: scaffold the iMessage overspend snitch bot

Wire one Bun process so a demo can roast overspending without extra services.
```

```
fix(poller): skip purchases already handled by the swipe page
```
